From 82c95122e10c7d14fe0188df3b5d192d392effbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 09:14:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 203/913] clk: stm32: enable new critical clock management

Use the CLK_IS_CRITICAL flag to mark clocks as critical.
Critical clocks are enabled at boot and must never be disabled.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 962626d86a5cac5d6db57599f53bcb0db45c72c8 clk: stm32: enable new critical clock management]
Signed-off-by: Gabriel Fernandez <gabriel.fernandez@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: If6fe42808d6e4ffcc18f37f902f4101408987638
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/545791
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Thomas BOURGOIN <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.c | 2 +-
 core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.h | 1 -
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.c b/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.c
index 955616e94..fac037ce0 100644
--- a/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.c
+++ b/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.c
@@ -662,7 +662,7 @@ static void clk_stm32_register_clocks(struct clk_stm32_priv *priv)
 		if (!clk)
 			continue;
 
-		if (priv->is_critical && priv->is_critical(clk))
+		if (clk->flags & CLK_IS_CRITICAL)
 			clk_enable(clk);
 	}
 }
diff --git a/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.h b/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.h
index f7b721647..4ddc6d2e7 100644
--- a/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.h
+++ b/core/drivers/clk/clk-stm32-core.h
@@ -46,7 +46,6 @@ struct clk_stm32_priv {
 	const uint32_t nb_gates;
 	const struct div_cfg *div;
 	const uint32_t nb_div;
-	bool (*is_critical)(struct clk *clk);
 	void *pdata;
 };
 
-- 
